# Keep Cursor's indexer out of Rust build artifacts.
#
# Why this file exists: the workspace `target/` grew to 52 GB (46 GB in
# `target/debug`, 17 GB of it `incremental/`, plus nine ~490 MB `libsyx_rt-*.a`
# duplicates). Cursor was indexing it, which pushed a 32 GB machine past 50 GB of
# memory and forced a hard kill mid-session.
#
# Git already ignores these paths (.gitignore `/target/`), but Cursor's indexer
# benefits from an explicit deny list, and file watching needs to skip them too.

target/
target-full-native/
**/target/

# Per-example build output (same class of problem, smaller scale).
examples/**/target/
examples/**/.syx-cache/
packages/.sy-cache/

# Test/scratch artifacts that churn constantly and are never worth indexing.
*.wasm
*.wat
*.a
*.rlib
*.dSYM/

# Local editor/agent scratch dirs.
.cursor/plans/archive/
